From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake/vcpkg/ports/pcre: disable JIT on riscv64

The build fails during `vcpkg install` of the `pcre` overlay port:

    pcre_jit_compile.c:65:2: error: #error Unsupported architecture
    ninja: build stopped: subcommand failed.
    error: building pcre:riscv64-linux failed with: BUILD_FAILED

This port vendors PCRE 8.45 (legacy PCRE1, last released 2021) with its own
bundled copy of sljit. That copy predates sljit's RISC-V work and ships no
`sljitNativeRISCV*.c` backend file at all (confirmed by listing
`sljit/sljitNative*.c` in the extracted PCRE 8.45 tarball: x86, ARM, MIPS,
PPC, SPARC, TILEGX - no RISC-V). `pcre_jit_compile.c`'s own
`SLJIT_CONFIG_AUTO` detection therefore falls through to
`SLJIT_CONFIG_UNSUPPORTED`, which the file turns into a hard `#error`. This
is unrelated to PCRE2's sljit fork, which did gain a real riscv64 JIT
backend - the two forks diverged well before that.

The port already disables JIT for other architectures its bundled sljit
doesn't cover (`loongarch`, `s390`, via `IS_PCRE_SUPPORT_JIT`); riscv64 just
isn't in that list because upstream has never built or published a riscv64
wheel. Add it, same as the existing entries, rather than trying to backport
a RISC-V sljit backend into a decade-old vendored copy for a feature (JIT)
cppcheck itself does not need.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [riscv64-only build fix for a package upstream does not build or test for riscv64; folds into the port's existing per-arch no-JIT list rather than changing behavior for any arch upstream supports]
---
 cmake/vcpkg/ports/pcre/portfile.cmake | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/vcpkg/ports/pcre/portfile.cmake b/cmake/vcpkg/ports/pcre/portfile.cmake
--- a/cmake/vcpkg/ports/pcre/portfile.cmake
+++ b/cmake/vcpkg/ports/pcre/portfile.cmake
@@ -22,7 +22,11 @@ vcpkg_from_sourceforge(
 )

 set(IS_PCRE_SUPPORT_JIT YES)
-if(VCPKG_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE MATCHES "(loongarch|^s390)")
+# riscv64: this port's vendored PCRE 8.45 JIT has no sljit backend for RISC-V at all (no
+# sljitNativeRISCV*.c, unlike PCRE2's newer, separately-maintained sljit fork), so
+# pcre_jit_compile.c's own `#if SLJIT_CONFIG_UNSUPPORTED ... #error Unsupported architecture`
+# always fires there. Added alongside the existing loongarch/s390 no-JIT arches.
+if(VCPKG_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE MATCHES "(loongarch|^s390|riscv64)")
     set(IS_PCRE_SUPPORT_JIT NO)
 endif()

--
